("ADJ-227","neat – neater – neatest","After 'very neat and', use the adjective 'organized', not the verb.","NEAT: short and tidy word.","Informal American 'Neat!' = great.","Write a sentence about someone with neat handwriting.",None,"neat vs clean","Clean = no dirt. Neat = tidy and well-arranged."),
("ADJ-228","messy – messier – messiest","Before an adjective, use 'too', not 'too much'.","MESSY: MESS + Y.","'A messy divorce' = a difficult, unpleasant one.","Write a sentence about the messiest place in your house.",None,"messy vs dirty","Dirty = has dirt. Messy = untidy."),
("ADJ-229","formal – more formal – most formal","'Formal' is an adjective. 'Formals' as a noun for clothes is Indian English.","FORMAL: follows the FORM (the rules).","Formal emails begin 'Dear Sir/Madam'.","Write a formal first line for an email to a company.",None,"formal vs official","Official = from an authority. Formal = following strict rules of style.","Please wear formals for the interview.","Please wear formal clothes for the interview."),
